| `eq-asio-driver` | `com.rs:8-11` registry/module path, `pacing.rs:26-29` QPC + waitable timer + MMCSS; features `Cargo.toml:14-24` | (c) stays Windows |

**Hard blocker found (verified):** the workspace has **zero** `cfg(windows)`/`cfg(unix)`/`target_os` gates, while every affected crate declares `windows = { workspace = true }` (`router-core/Cargo.toml:10`, `router-engine:14`, `router-cli:18`, `bridge-abi:10`, `eq-asio-app:18`, `eq-asio-driver:14`, `asio-host:10`, `asio-probe:11`, `wasapi-capture:*** The `windows` crate is `#![cfg(windows)]` (`…/windows-0.62.2/src/lib.rs` crate root) — an **empty stub** on unix/mac targets — so every `use windows::…` site (~40 in router-engine/router-core/router-cli alone) fails to resolve off-Windows. Consequence: `cargo check --workspace --target …` cannot pass until gating lands (see A.7).

### A.2 Architecture decision (deliverable 2)

**DECIDED: write a new thin `portable-engine` crate** reusing `eq-core` + `router-core` primitives; do not port `router-engine` behind traits. The plan's lean (Phase A section above) is confirmed against the code:

- `router-engine` is ~6.7k lines; the Windows-entangled core is exactly the parts that don't port:
  - `priority.rs` — 360 lines, ~100% MMCSS/timer (b).
  - `engine.rs` control thread = STA message pump: `pump_wait` runs every iteration of the session loop (`engine.rs:1141-1218`), single-instance mutex `engine.rs:182-208`, `Session` bound to `AsioDriver` (`engine.rs:540-605`, ASIO teardown in `Drop`), ~365 lines of ASIO bring-up in `Session::open` (`engine.rs:606-970`: rate negotiation `:626-635`, `choose_buffer_size` call `:638`, sample-type/channel setup `:644-652`, bridge shm attach `:665-690`).
  - `pipeline.rs` render core (`Pipeline`, `:342-578`) **is** portable except QPC clock `:143-160`, MMCSS `:414`, and the ASIO output adapter (`OutputSet`/`PtrTable` `:174-238`, `Handler` impl `:583-669`, ≈90 lines) — the adapter is the natural `OutputSink` seam origin.
- Reusable as-is: `logic.rs` (521 lines, 0 Win32: `choose_buffer_size` `:202`, back-off, burst estimate, capacity planning), `status.rs` (302, 0 Win32), `tap.rs` (189), `baseline.rs` (817), `bridge.rs` state machine (687, 0 Win32 imports — its *source role* is Windows-only), `pipeline_tests.rs`.
- Structural argument: because **no `cfg(windows)` exists anywhere** (A.1), "port behind traits" would first require gating ~40 `use windows::…` sites across router-engine/router-core/router-cli — that gating *is* most of the port — and the gated-out remainder (STA pump, single-instance, ASIO session, MMCSS) is the Windows shell the portable app replaces anyway. A new crate gets a clean cfg/feature story for the B1/B2 wave that retrofitting cannot.

**OPEN for Phase B:** relocation of `router-engine/src/logic.rs` (portable, 0 Win32) — move to `router-core`, copy into `portable-engine`, or re-implement; must be a single-owner decision (see A.6).

### A.3 Seams (deliverable 3) — trait sketches, signatures only

```rust
// portable-engine/src/seams.rs
pub struct StreamFormat { pub rate: u32, pub period_frames: u32, pub channels: u16 }

pub trait OutputSink {                       // origin: asio_host::Handler (asio-host/src/lib.rs:141)
    fn negotiate(&mut self, want: &StreamFormat) -> Result<StreamFormat, Error>;
    //   <- caps probe + choose_buffer_size (router-engine/src/engine.rs:638, logic.rs:202)
    fn start(&mut self, cb: Box<dyn FnMut(OutputBuf<'_>) + Send>) -> Result<(), Error>;
    //   <- AudioCallback::run (pipeline.rs:607), event-driven at negotiated period
    fn stop(&mut self);                      //   <- Session teardown (engine.rs:567-604)
}
pub struct OutputBuf<'a> { pub out: &'a mut [&mut [f32]], pub frames: usize, pub t: i64 }

pub trait SystemSource {                    // producer side of the SPSC ring
    fn pump(&mut self) -> Result<u32, Error>;        // -> ring::Producer (router-core/ring.rs)
    fn stats(&self) -> ArrivalSnapshot;             // <- router_core::arrival::ArrivalStats (arrival.rs:111)
}
pub trait Clock   { fn now(&self) -> i64; fn freq(&self) -> i64; }   // <- qpc()/qpc_freq() (pipeline.rs:143/155)
pub trait StatusTransport { fn publisher(&self) -> Option<Box<dyn StatusPub>>; }
                                                    // <- StatusWriter (router-core/status_writer.rs:80) + eq-core/status.rs layout
pub trait ControlLoop {                             // <- pump_wait (engine.rs:210) / control_loop (engine.rs:1021)
    fn wait(&mut self, d: Duration) -> bool;        //   condvar/recv_timeout off-Windows
    fn run(&mut self, cmds: Receiver<Cmd>) -> Result<(), Error>;
}
```

Mapping of existing types onto the seams (verified at the cited lines):

| Existing type | Seam / role | Portability |
|---|---|---|
| `FrameSource` (`router-core/resample.rs:19`) | input to `RateMatcher` / `SystemSource` producer | portable as-is |
| `ArrivalStats` (`router-core/arrival.rs:111`) | `SystemSource::stats` | portable as-is |
| `Handoff<T>` (`router-core/processor.rs:121`) | snapshot publish across RT/control | portable as-is |

